<title>POLAND: POLISH PBI BANK CUTS ZLOTY AND CURRENCY DEPO RATES.</title>
<headline>POLISH PBI BANK CUTS ZLOTY AND CURRENCY DEPO RATES.</headline>
<dateline>WARSAW 1997-02-28</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Polish Investment Bank (PBI) will cut its term zloty deposit rates by between 0.5 and one point and call and term currency deposit rates by 0.1 to 0.9 point on March 1, PBI's spokeswoman said on Friday.</p>
<p>Anna Rybaltowska told Reuters the move was a result of the National Bank of Poland's decision to raise banks' obligatory resreves by three points to 20 percent on zloty deposits and by two points to four percent on currency deposits as of today.</p>
<p>-- Warsaw Newsroom +48 22 653 9700</p>
